From 382bfc199fcf942699f330e19ab16d8c9051b084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:46:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XHCI X4: bulk + interrupt transfer rings

Bulk endpoints (EP context type 2 OUT / 6 IN) execute Normal-TRB
chains on their doorbell: CH-linked TRBs stream through the U1-U5
mass-storage model and the chain completes with exactly one Transfer
Event, as the guest issues it (xhci.c:1636-1727 -- IOC on the last
TRB only). A short IN chain stops serving further TRBs and completes
cc 13 Short Packet with byte residue; OUT chains take their bytes.
Direction is the endpoint type (Normal TRBs carry none).

The BOT engine in devices.c gains an exported front door,
usb_stick_serve(m, ctl, pid, total, buf) in devices.h, with ctl
selecting per-controller state (0 EHCI, 1 UHCI, 2 XHCI -- a new third
instance, snapshot-tagged dev.usb.bot.xhci). The guest's BOT dialogue
is three bulk transfers (CBW OUT 31, data, CSW IN 13), so xHCI now
answers TEST UNIT READY, INQUIRY, READ CAPACITY and READ(10)/(12)
byte-identically to the EHCI/UHCI lanes, inherited limits included
(medium-absent FAILED, PHASE on a malformed CBW, no WRITE opcodes).
Endpoint dequeue pointers are mirrored into the output contexts.

Interrupt endpoints follow the guest's non-blocking poll contract
(xhci.c:1731-1868): it arms one Normal TRB and treats "no event" as
the idle answer. This machine has no HID device model on any bus
(the keyboard is PS/2), so an interrupt TRB stays armed and
unconsumed -- NAK, never a fabricated report -- while the other
endpoints keep answering; isochronous TRBs likewise remain queued
(the guest's isoch lane is U9, our X5+ ledger).

tests/test_xhci.c gains two groups (19 total): a full BOT dialogue
against a known 8-sector image (TUR absent/present, INQUIRY vendor,
READ CAPACITY geometry, a 2-sector READ(10) across a CH chain with
the single-event property asserted, short-read cc13 + CSW residue
agreement, malformed-CBW PHASE) and the armed-interrupt contract.
NC: src/xhci.c reverted to X3 -> 32 failures. Gates: make test,
make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.
